# What claude-test.sh runs: one Claude session per layout (reachable, top), the plan's cases, and each session's bounds.
# entries-<layout> tells that session which directory entries and names its cases use, so none meets an entry already known.
model: claude-haiku-5-5
layouts: reachable top
cases: all of the plan's cases (C1-C9, D1-D15, U1-U3, N1-N11, W1-W11, G1-G4) and the full search, skipping those named under "How to run the cases"
entries-reachable: D6 joins ci_channel, which U1 then searches by name and U2 by "seed channel"; W6 joins ci_avatar_c2; D11 searches "private" (only the local chat "Private notes" has it); D14 and D15 use a second profile you add, which N7 then uses; N10 connects to @cialice.testing, which N5, W7 and G1 then use; W8 first connects to @cibobby.testing (Robert) from its Names row
entries-top: D6 joins ci_avatar_c1, which U1 then searches by name and U2 by "avatar channel 1"; W6 joins ci_avatar_c3; D11 searches "private"; D14, D15 and N7 use the second profile from the earlier session (add one if it is missing); the contacts cialice and Robert are already connected (N5, W7, W8, G1 use them); N10 taps the Names row of the channel #ciboth.testing
max-turns: 900
max-budget-usd: 10
